Li forms normal oxide (Li₂O);
Na forms peroxide (Na₂O₂);
K, Rb, and Cs form superoxides (KO₂, RbO₂, CsO₂).

Electrical work done by cell = -ΔG
ΔG = -n · F · E_{cell}
Under standard state conditions:
ΔG° = -n · F · E°_{cell}
where n = moles of electrons transferred in balanced cell reaction, and F = Faraday constant (≈ 96500 C mol⁻¹).
For a spontaneous process: E_{cell} > 0 and ΔG < 0.
